00:50:19.860 --> 00:50:23.299
and many doctors and nurses and scientists are asking the question, so it's really important we

00:50:23.299 --> 00:50:26.589
understand, but that at this stage we're saying
there's no long-term lasting effects.

00:50:26.589 --> 00:50:30.509
That's a really good question.  What we
have found, which is really amazing,

00:50:30.509 --> 00:50:36.200
is that we have found that the virus in men,
even though it's not found in their blood,

00:50:36.230 --> 00:50:42.490
the virus can be found in their semen.  And
so what we're recommending now if a man gets infected,

00:50:42.780 --> 00:50:48.140
he shouldn't have sex (or, if he
has sex, he has to use a condom) for at

00:50:48.150 --> 00:50:51.510
least six months. and that's the
recommendation for the Center for

00:50:51.510 --> 00:50:54.510
Disease Control right now.  It might
change as we learn more.

00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:10.440
Okay.  My question was, um, what are the likely fatality rates of babies who are infected with Zika?

00:51:11.640 --> 00:51:14.440
That's a really good
question.  And we know that we have about -

00:51:14.450 --> 00:51:18.180
in the United States
every year about four million babies are

00:51:18.180 --> 00:51:24.420
born every year.  We know that even before
Zika, there's about 2,500 of those babies that

00:51:24.420 --> 00:51:29.200
have microcephaly.  We have many years of information, many years of data shows that

00:51:29.200 --> 00:51:33.930
2,500 out of about four million babies born
every year.  Many of those babies go on

00:51:33.930 --> 00:51:40.079
and have normal lives.  Many of those
babies have, maybe, some

00:51:40.079 --> 00:51:46.659
developmental problems, but it's not
severe.  When you have severe microcephaly,

00:51:46.660 --> 00:51:51.120
like a Down syndrome baby, they
need support for the rest of their life.

00:51:51.130 --> 00:51:54.180
And so it's really important that

00:51:54.180 --> 00:51:58.390
what we're seeing now is that, even some
babies are born with small-sized heads

00:51:58.390 --> 00:52:03.400
at birth, are actually doing okay.  There're doing well.  They're not having long lasting effects.  But there's

00:52:03.400 --> 00:52:08.700
other babies have severe microcephaly, severe small sized heads, which means they have severe small

00:52:08.700 --> 00:52:13.790
size brains, and they need support.  And
they're having also other problems -problems with

00:52:13.790 --> 00:52:17.210
their eyes, problems with their vision,
problems with their growth, problems with their

00:52:17.210 --> 00:52:21.329
balance, and it's really important that
we have the programs in place to support

00:52:21.329 --> 00:52:24.960
those babies, support those moms and dads and those families.  That's what's really

00:52:24.960 --> 00:52:28.200
important.  So we're really worried about
this in countries where we're seeing an

00:52:28.200 --> 00:52:33.020
increased number of microcephaly, does
the program at the hospital or community - are those

00:52:33.020 --> 00:52:36.770
programs in place to support those moms
and dads with a baby that needs a lot of

00:52:36.770 --> 00:52:38.790
support?  And that doesn't always happen.

00:52:43.060 --> 00:52:44.480
We have a question from Hawaii.

00:52:44.900 --> 00:52:51.640
Do you think that, just like the influenza, the Zika virus can go through mutations, since some cases of Zika are different from another?

00:52:52.600 --> 00:52:55.640
Yeah, that's a great question.  Because again, this is what was called an

00:52:55.640 --> 00:53:00.190
RNA virus, and we know that with all
these RNA virus, they mutate.

00:53:00.190 --> 00:53:04.190
They change a million times a day.  Does
that mean anything?  We don't really know.

00:53:04.190 --> 00:53:07.829
Does it make them more
infectious?  Does it change the outcome in babies?

00:53:07.829 --> 00:53:12.240
Not really.  But with we're monitoring this.
So it's really important that we have

00:53:12.240 --> 00:53:15.520
we have laboratories, we have
universities, we have scientists that are

00:53:15.520 --> 00:53:19.590
monitoring the Zika virus in many
countries, because the big concern is that

00:53:19.590 --> 00:53:22.670
it's gone to nearly sixty countries now
since 2007.

00:53:23.270 --> 00:53:27.970
It's gone to nearly 45 countries in the
last 12 months.  So it's going through

00:53:27.970 --> 00:53:30.330
that cycle of mosquito to people,

00:53:30.330 --> 00:53:34.880
mosquito to people and, every time it goes through that cycle, it has a chance to mutate.

00:53:34.880 --> 00:53:39.960
And it's really important that we stay on
top of this to monitor any mutations.

00:53:39.960 --> 00:53:43.720
If we find a mutation, then we had to do
more research and understand what does

00:53:43.730 --> 00:53:47.430
that mutation mean.  So again, this is a
concern we had.  This is one of the

00:53:47.430 --> 00:53:53.600
hypothesis.  This is one of the ideas that was posed back in Brazil last year in May 2015

00:53:53.600 --> 00:53:59.090
when Brazil said, "Hey we got increased cases of Zika in people, increased cases of microcephaly, small

00:53:59.090 --> 00:54:04.310
sized babies being born with small heads."
We didn't know whether it was because of a

00:54:04.310 --> 00:54:09.040
mutation, and we're not, and so we are still
studying now.  And we can do this with what's called

00:54:09.040 --> 00:54:12.640
through genomics sequencing.  We do a
fingerprint of the virus and we see whether

00:54:12.640 --> 00:54:17.300
the virus has mutated.  And again, we have
to work at if that mutation actually is

00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:21.300
going to cause any problems, and that's what researchers do every day right now.

00:54:27.300 --> 00:54:36.480
Well, from King Drew we'd like to thank you Dr. Macgregor.  It's coming to the conclusion of our presentation for today.

00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:38.200
Would you guys like to say something?

00:54:38.480 --> 00:54:40.980
Thank you.

00:54:41.600 --> 00:54:43.600
You're very welcome.

00:54:44.520 --> 00:54:47.580
Thank you for warning us and giving us what we can do, right?

00:54:51.600 --> 00:54:52.720
Also from Hawaii -

00:54:53.100 --> 00:54:56.680
thank you.  Thank you.

00:54:59.800 --> 00:55:00.680
We learned a lot.

00:55:01.280 --> 00:55:01.860
Thanks.

00:55:02.920 --> 00:55:05.120
You're very welcome.

